  $$
  Thus, \(m = \frac{5 \pm 1}{2} \implies m = 3 \text{ or } 2\).

Therefore, the only solutions are \((m, n) = (2, 1)\) and \((m, n) = (3, 1)\).

By symmetry, we also have \((m, n) = (1, 2)\) and \((m, n) = (1, 3)\).

