(c - 2)m^2 = 1 \implies -m^2 = 1 \implies m^2 = 1 \implies m = 1.
\]
Thus, \(m = n = 1\) is a solution. We now show that \((1, 1)\) is the only solution. Assume \(m \neq n\). Then, from the quadratic in \(m\):
\[
