so \( 2^r p \notin S \).

Therefore, the only \( n = 2^k p \) such that \( \sum_{d \mid n, d < n, d \in S} d = n \) is when \( k = a \), where \( a = \lfloor \log_2(p+1) \rfloor - 1 \).

